Currently, elysia-compression hardcoded response headers which means the header in `set` will be ignored.

```ts
return app.onAfterHandle((_, res) => {
  const buf = Buffer.from(JSON.stringify(res),)
  const compressed = Bun.gzipSync(buf, options)  

  return new Response(compressed, {
    // hardcoded headers, set.headers is ignored
    headers: {
      'Content-Encoding': 'gzip',
    }
  })
})
```

This PR patch the behavior described above by using this code instead:
```ts
return app.onAfterHandle(({ set }, res) => {
    set.headers['Content-Encoding'] = 'gzip'

    return new Response(gzipSync(toBuffer(res), options), set)
})
```

This PR also adds the following:
- CommonJS build for Nodejs compatibility
- Basic test case to test encoding header and `set.headers`
- CHANGELOG.md

